      "prompt": "You are trading-risk-reviewer running the Q3\u2192Q4 promotion review.\n\n## Task\nEvaluate whether Weekend Short 1m (strategy 29) and US Session Open Short 1h (strategy 34) pass the >57% WR gate for paper-arena promotion.\n\nThe script's stdout (below the --- DATA --- marker) contains live DB queries for both strategies covering Q3 2026 (Jul 1 - Sep 30).\n\n## Gate Requirements (from task t_5a1fbb5e)\nBoth strategies must pass ALL conditions for promotion:\n\n### Weekend Short 1m (strategy 29)\n1. Q3 win rate >57%, net-of-fee (clean_outcome_binary_24h ~ 12bps baked in)\n2. Temporal stability across Q3 months (no single month <45% WR)\n3. Sufficient sample: >=500 labeled SHORT signals, and at least some 1m signals (the 1m pipeline was fixed in July, verify it produced data)\n4. Leak-free, signal-time-only (already verified at registration)\n\n### US Session Open Short 1h (strategy 34)\n1. Q3 win rate >57%, net-of-fee\n2. Temporal stability across Q3 months (no single month <45% WR)\n3. Sufficient sample: >=200 labeled Q3 signals\n\n## Decision matrix\n- **BOTH pass**: Create a kanban child task for paper-trader to prepare paper-arena promotion packet. Do NOT enable live trading, do NOT insert trade_intents. Recommend paper-arena onboarding.\n- **Either fails**: Document no-promotion rationale. Create a monitoring/research follow-up task for the failing strategy.\n- **Insufficient data** (e.g. 1m pipeline still dead for strategy 29): Return INCONCLUSIVE with explanation.\n\n## Safety gates\n- Paper mode only. No live trading, no production deploy, no secrets, no irreversible ops.\n- If promotion recommended, child task goes to `paper-trader` profile.\n- If monitor/research needed, child task goes to `trading-data-oracle` profile.\n\n## Output format\nFirst line: VERDICT=PROMOTE | VERDICT=NO_PROMOTION | VERDICT=INCONCLUSIVE\nThen 1-3 paragraphs of evidence and reasoning.\nIf promoting, include: \"CHILD_TASK_NEEDED: paper-trader \u2014 paper-arena promotion packet for strategies [list ids]\".\nIf not promoting: describe what follow-up task is needed and its assignee.\n",
